WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:03.962
I would give a first generation low
income student in high school the advice,

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.588
Just relax.

00:00:05.588 --> 00:00:07.757
You're going to be okay
and you're going to end up

00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:10.927
where you're supposed to be.
For a lot of FGLI students.

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:14.222
Something that comes up is imposter
syndrome.

00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:17.475
Really practice in
building self confidence

00:00:17.475 --> 00:00:21.521
and really believing in yourself,
knowing that you are just as capable.

00:00:21.646 --> 00:00:24.858
My best advice is to just be yourself.

00:00:24.941 --> 00:00:27.986
There's really no mold
that we want you to fit into.

00:00:28.153 --> 00:00:30.363
We're looking for people
who are authentic.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:32.657
I would say apply through QuestBridge.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:38.288
I found the QuestBridge application
was really a valuable tool for me

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:41.750
because it allowed me to present my story
and who I am

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.836
more than just, you know, what
I've done academically.

00:00:45.295 --> 00:00:48.423
Look for what you're going
to bring to the community here at Yale

00:00:48.423 --> 00:00:51.509
and how it's going to serve you
just as well as you're going to serve it.

00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:55.597
Focusing on that rather than making
yourself into somebody that you're not

00:00:55.805 --> 00:00:57.223
is definitely the right way to go.

